IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pbha-holidays`

-- Public and Bank Holidays Act 1972 (WA) -- the Q&A layer: the questions people ask about WA's public and bank holidays,
-- with the seat and the situation as parameters, for one deployment that serves every seat. (The daydate library is
-- imported by the baseline module, as before; this layer needs none of its functions.)
--
-- ROLES (the seat as a parameter). Every exported question takes `my role` first ("Which of these describes you"). A question
-- about another role answers `does not arise for you` without reading any other input, so the form never asks those inputs.
--   - `I work in Western Australia` -- the baseline's seat, the employee.
--   - `I employ people in Western Australia` -- new: which days are public holidays for the workplace, and how a WA
--     industrial instrument the employer is party to stands against the Act (ss 3, 9).
--   - `I run a bank, or a bank branch, in Western Australia` -- new: s 10 puts the one duty in the Act on "all banks in the
--     State": to close their premises to the public on bank holidays.
-- The Governor is never a seat: a proclamation under s 7 or s 8 is a fact the person states from the Gazette.
-- The calendar questions (on what day a holiday falls, the year's list and count, which holidays fall on a day, whether a
-- day is a bank holiday) are asked by all three roles; whether a day is a public holiday where the work is done, and the
-- industrial instrument questions, by the employee and the employer.
--
-- SITUATIONS (the graffiti design D8). Within a role, a question that arises only in a situation takes that situation's fact
-- straight after `my role`, and answers `does not arise for you` without reading anything else when the situation does not
-- hold. The questions of one situation share one input, with the same name, type and @desc:
--   - `a WA industrial instrument covers the work` (BOOLEAN; employee and employer): s 3 speaks only of "an industrial
--     instrument" (an award, order or agreement made under the Industrial Relations Act 1979 (WA), or an employer-employee
--     agreement), so FALSE gives `does not arise for you` for the two s 3 questions.
--   - `I work in a bank` (BOOLEAN; employee): s 10 binds banks, so for an employee the closing question arises only for one
--     who works in a bank. FALSE gives `does not arise for you`. The bank's own closing question arises for every bank.
--
-- The rules are the baseline's (`pbha-holidays.l4`); this layer calls them and restates none. Where the employee asks a
-- question here, the answer is the baseline export's, wrapped in the answer type. No exported question takes a DEONTIC or
-- EVENT input.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Public and Bank Holidays Act 1972 (WA) -- the questions people ask`

§§ `Who is asking, and the shape of the answers`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `I work in Western Australia`
    `I employ people in Western Australia`
    `I run a bank, or a bank branch, in Western Australia`

DECLARE `Yes or no` IS ONE OF
    yes
    no
    `does not arise for you`

DECLARE `Day of a holiday` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the holiday` HAS `when it falls` IS A `When it falls`

DECLARE `Days` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the days` HAS `the dates` IS A LIST OF DATE

DECLARE `Count` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `count` HAS `how many` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Holidays on a day` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the holidays` HAS `which` IS A LIST OF Holiday

DECLARE `Public holiday or not` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `public holiday` HAS `the answer` IS A `Public holiday answer`

DECLARE `What prevails` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `prevails` HAS `which` IS A `Which prevails`

GIVEN `it holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`yes if` `it holds` MEANS
    IF `it holds` THEN yes ELSE no

§§ `For everyone: the calendar (s 5, Second Schedule, s 6)`

@export On what day does this public holiday fall in WA in a given year (Public and Bank Holidays Act 1972 (WA) s 5, Second Schedule)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the holiday` IS A Holiday @desc Which holiday in the Second Schedule, or which weekend extra day
      `the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year, for example 2024
      `the Sovereign's birthday as proclaimed` IS A DATE @desc The day appointed for that year by proclamation in the Government Gazette for the King's Birthday, ISO 8601
GIVETH A `Day of a holiday`
`On what day does this public holiday fall in WA` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work in Western Australia` THEN `the holiday` (`On what day does this holiday fall` `the holiday` `the year` `the Sovereign's birthday as proclaimed`)
    WHEN `I employ people in Western Australia` THEN `the holiday` (`On what day does this holiday fall` `the holiday` `the year` `the Sovereign's birthday as proclaimed`)
    WHEN `I run a bank, or a bank branch, in Western Australia` THEN `the holiday` (`On what day does this holiday fall` `the holiday` `the year` `the Sovereign's birthday as proclaimed`)

@export What are the public holidays in WA in a given year, as dates (Public and Bank Holidays Act 1972 (WA) s 5, Second Schedule)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year, for example 2024
      `the Sovereign's birthday as proclaimed` IS A DATE @desc The day appointed for that year by proclamation in the Government Gazette for the King's Birthday, ISO 8601
GIVETH A `Days`
`What are the public holidays in WA in this year` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work in Western Australia` THEN `the days` (`What are the public holidays in WA this year` `the year` `the Sovereign's birthday as proclaimed`)
    WHEN `I employ people in Western Australia` THEN `the days` (`What are the public holidays in WA this year` `the year` `the Sovereign's birthday as proclaimed`)
    WHEN `I run a bank, or a bank branch, in Western Australia` THEN `the days` (`What are the public holidays in WA this year` `the year` `the Sovereign's birthday as proclaimed`)

@export How many days are public holidays in WA in a given year under the Schedule (Public and Bank Holidays Act 1972 (WA) s 5, Second Schedule)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year, for example 2024
      `the Sovereign's birthday as proclaimed` IS A DATE @desc The day appointed for that year by proclamation in the Government Gazette for the King's Birthday, ISO 8601
GIVETH A `Count`
`How many days are public holidays in WA in this year` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work in Western Australia` THEN `count` (`How many public holidays in WA this year` `the year` `the Sovereign's birthday as proclaimed`)
    WHEN `I employ people in Western Australia` THEN `count` (`How many public holidays in WA this year` `the year` `the Sovereign's birthday as proclaimed`)
    WHEN `I run a bank, or a bank branch, in Western Australia` THEN `count` (`How many public holidays in WA this year` `the year` `the Sovereign's birthday as proclaimed`)

@export Which Schedule holidays fall on this day in WA (Public and Bank Holidays Act 1972 (WA) s 5, Second Schedule)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day, ISO 8601
      `the Sovereign's birthday as proclaimed` IS A DATE @desc The day appointed for that year by proclamation in the Government Gazette for the King's Birthday, ISO 8601
GIVETH A `Holidays on a day`
`Which Schedule holidays fall on this day in WA` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work in Western Australia` THEN `the holidays` (`Which holidays fall on this day` `the day` `the Sovereign's birthday as proclaimed`)
    WHEN `I employ people in Western Australia` THEN `the holidays` (`Which holidays fall on this day` `the day` `the Sovereign's birthday as proclaimed`)
    WHEN `I run a bank, or a bank branch, in Western Australia` THEN `the holidays` (`Which holidays fall on this day` `the day` `the Sovereign's birthday as proclaimed`)

@export Is this day a bank holiday in WA (Public and Bank Holidays Act 1972 (WA) ss 5, 6)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day, ISO 8601
      `the Sovereign's birthday as proclaimed` IS A DATE @desc The day appointed for that year by proclamation in the Government Gazette for the King's Birthday, ISO 8601
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is this day a bank holiday in Western Australia` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work in Western Australia` THEN `yes if` (`Is this day a bank holiday in WA` `the day` `the Sovereign's birthday as proclaimed`)
    WHEN `I employ people in Western Australia` THEN `yes if` (`Is this day a bank holiday in WA` `the day` `the Sovereign's birthday as proclaimed`)
    WHEN `I run a bank, or a bank branch, in Western Australia` THEN `yes if` (`Is this day a bank holiday in WA` `the day` `the Sovereign's birthday as proclaimed`)

§§ `For the employee and the employer`

§§§ `ss 5, 7, 8 -- is this day a public holiday where the work is done`

@export Is this day a public holiday in WA for the place where I work, or where my employees work (Public and Bank Holidays Act 1972 (WA) ss 5, 7, 8)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day, ISO 8601
      `the Sovereign's birthday as proclaimed` IS A DATE @desc The day appointed for that year by proclamation in the Government Gazette for the King's Birthday, ISO 8601
      `a s 7 proclamation makes this day a special public holiday at the workplace` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Governor has by proclamation under s 7 appointed this day a special public holiday, throughout the State or in the district where the work is done
      `a s 8 proclamation makes this day a public holiday instead of a Schedule day at the workplace` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Governor has by proclamation under s 8 declared this day a public holiday in place of a Schedule day, for the place where the work is done
      `a s 8 proclamation moves this day's holiday to another day at the workplace` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Governor has by proclamation under s 8 moved the Schedule holiday on this day to some other day, for the place where the work is done
GIVETH A `Public holiday or not`
`Is this day a public holiday where the work is done` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work in Western Australia` THEN `public holiday` (`Is this day a public holiday for me in WA` `the day` `the Sovereign's birthday as proclaimed` `a s 7 proclamation makes this day a special public holiday at the workplace` `a s 8 proclamation makes this day a public holiday instead of a Schedule day at the workplace` `a s 8 proclamation moves this day's holiday to another day at the workplace`)
    WHEN `I employ people in Western Australia` THEN `public holiday` (`Is this day a public holiday for me in WA` `the day` `the Sovereign's birthday as proclaimed` `a s 7 proclamation makes this day a special public holiday at the workplace` `a s 8 proclamation makes this day a public holiday instead of a Schedule day at the workplace` `a s 8 proclamation moves this day's holiday to another day at the workplace`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 3, 9 -- a WA industrial instrument against the Act`

@export Does the WA industrial instrument, the Act, or a proclamation prevail on public holidays (Public and Bank Holidays Act 1972 (WA) ss 3, 9)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `a WA industrial instrument covers the work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an award, order or industrial agreement made under the Industrial Relations Act 1979 (WA), or an employer-employee agreement, covers the work (not a Fair Work Act 2009 award or agreement)
      `the instrument is inconsistent with the provision of or under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the instrument says something different from the Act (or a proclamation under it) about the day
      `that provision is in a proclamation under s 7 or 8` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Act-side provision is a proclamation of the Governor under s 7 or s 8
      `the instrument substitutes another day for Easter Sunday solely because it falls on a weekend` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the inconsistency is that the instrument moves the Easter Sunday holiday to another day only because it is on a weekend
GIVETH A `What prevails`
`Does the industrial instrument or the Act prevail on public holidays` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work in Western Australia` THEN
        IF NOT `a WA industrial instrument covers the work`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `prevails` (`Does my award or this Act prevail` TRUE `the instrument is inconsistent with the provision of or under the Act` `that provision is in a proclamation under s 7 or 8` `the instrument substitutes another day for Easter Sunday solely because it falls on a weekend`)
    WHEN `I employ people in Western Australia` THEN
        IF NOT `a WA industrial instrument covers the work`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `prevails` (`Does my award or this Act prevail` TRUE `the instrument is inconsistent with the provision of or under the Act` `that provision is in a proclamation under s 7 or 8` `the instrument substitutes another day for Easter Sunday solely because it falls on a weekend`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Does the WA industrial instrument's public holiday provision apply to Easter Sunday (Public and Bank Holidays Act 1972 (WA) s 3(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `a WA industrial instrument covers the work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an award, order or industrial agreement made under the Industrial Relations Act 1979 (WA), or an employer-employee agreement, covers the work (not a Fair Work Act 2009 award or agreement)
      `the instrument has a provision relating to public holidays` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the instrument has any provision about public holidays (penalty rates, days off, and so on)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does the instrument's public holiday provision apply to Easter Sunday` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work in Western Australia` THEN
        IF NOT `a WA industrial instrument covers the work`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Does my award's public holiday provision apply to Easter Sunday` TRUE `the instrument has a provision relating to public holidays`)
    WHEN `I employ people in Western Australia` THEN
        IF NOT `a WA industrial instrument covers the work`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Does my award's public holiday provision apply to Easter Sunday` TRUE `the instrument has a provision relating to public holidays`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `s 10 -- banks closing to the public`

@export Must the bank where I work close its premises to the public on this day (Public and Bank Holidays Act 1972 (WA) s 10)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I work in a bank` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you work in a bank in Western Australia
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day, ISO 8601
      `the Sovereign's birthday as proclaimed` IS A DATE @desc The day appointed for that year by proclamation in the Government Gazette for the King's Birthday, ISO 8601
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must the bank where I work close to the public on this day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work in Western Australia` THEN
        IF NOT `I work in a bank`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Must my bank close to the public on this day` `the day` `the Sovereign's birthday as proclaimed`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- New for the bank: the same s 10 rule, asked as the bank's own duty. s 10(2) frees the bank on a Saturday that is a bank
-- holiday only by s 6, which the baseline's rule already gives.
@export Must I close my bank's premises to the public on this day (Public and Bank Holidays Act 1972 (WA) s 10)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day, ISO 8601
      `the Sovereign's birthday as proclaimed` IS A DATE @desc The day appointed for that year by proclamation in the Government Gazette for the King's Birthday, ISO 8601
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I close my bank's premises to the public on this day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I run a bank, or a bank branch, in Western Australia` THEN `yes if` (`Must my bank close to the public on this day` `the day` `the Sovereign's birthday as proclaimed`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`
